From 0733ddaad46cab62bd9990ceb235d95f8f1fa45d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omalawn <omalawn@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:45:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omalawn screen: read and operate the screen over the link

Lawnchair's accessibility service declares window content, gestures,
screenshots and interactive windows, keeps the serviceInfo built from its XML
(it used to replace it and drop the flags) and describes honestly what it
lets a paired computer do. screen.* (tree, tap, long_press, swipe, type, key,
shot, launch, status) is reachable by pinned link peers only; the shell-only
provider offers screen_status. launcher.ping no longer creates the device
profile (db is null until the home screen is open).
launcher.request_media_permission reports whether the wallpaper can be read
and, where a prompt can fix it (Android 12 and older), posts a notification
whose tap opens the system prompt; Android 13+ answers not_grantable.
---
